# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# FootyPredict environment variables
#
# RAPIDAPI key handling (server-side only — never shipped to the browser):
#
#   PRODUCTION (Vercel):
#     The Vercel serverless functions in /api (see lib/rapidapi.ts) read the
#     key from the runtime environment. Set it in Vercel → Project Settings →
#     Environment Variables. It CANNOT be defined in vercel.json.
#
#       RAPIDAPI_KEY=your-rapidapi-key-here
#       PREDICTIONS_KEY=fallback-key  (optional alias)
#
#   LOCAL DEV (`npm run dev`):
#     The dev server executes the /api functions locally via the shim in
#     scripts/vite-api-dev.ts. Drop the keys into this file (copied to `.env`,
#     which is gitignored) and they are read server-side ONLY — variables
#     without the VITE_ prefix are never inlined into the client bundle.
#
#       RAPIDAPI_KEY=your-rapidapi-key-here
#
#   Without a key, the functions still respond with a JSON error ("API key
#   not configured") instead of the app falling back to sample data — useful
#   for confirming the API layer is wired up.
#
# PAYSTACK_SECRET_KEY — same server-side rules; consumed by
# api/paystack-verify.ts to verify transactions before premium is granted:
#
#   PAYSTACK_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_xxx   (sk_live_xxx in production)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Legacy client-side fallback key for static hosts WITHOUT serverless
# functions (e.g. GitHub Pages), where the CORS-proxy path in
# src/services/apiClient.ts is used instead. WARNING: this bakes the key into
# the public JS bundle — use only as a last resort. The public proxies listed
# there also strip or block custom headers, so this path is unreliable.
# VITE_RAPIDAPI_KEY=

# Optional Paystack public key override for the checkout page.
# VITE_PAYSTACK_PUBLIC_KEY=
